sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Project Lead / External Adversary
    participant P as Route 53 Parent DNS
    participant C as Route 53 Child DNS
    participant W as Public Web Target
    participant S as Splunk Enterprise
    participant L as AI Bridge
    participant SOC as SOC Analyst
    participant IR as IR / Defender

    Note over A,SOC: Adversary uses separate AWS account / optional external Windows. SOC is not told start time, source IP or commands.
    A->>P: Public lookup for lab namespace
    P-->>A: Child NS referral where applicable
    A->>C: A / AAAA / MX / NS / TXT / likely-name DNS reconnaissance
    C-->>A: Authoritative DNS responses
    A->>C: Optional AXFR check
    A->>W: Optional non-destructive HTTP / HTTPS follow-up
    C-->>S: Route 53 authoritative query logs via collection pipeline
    W-->>S: Nginx / network telemetry
    S->>S: Detection v1.0 / scheduled alert
    S->>L: Webhook alert evidence
    L-->>S: AI-assisted context via HEC
    SOC->>S: Validate raw evidence / history / correlations
    SOC->>IR: Evidence-backed escalation when warranted
    IR->>IR: Human-approved response / verification if required
    Note over A,IR: Ground truth is revealed only after SOC disposition and IR handoff are locked.
